QuestGuidance.Register("en",47,{
[1473]="700529A2\n1\tCollect restless bones (total: 10)\tAudvak asked you to collect restless bones from Avabárg so she might give them proper burials.\n",
[1474]="70026F04\n1\tTalk to Harri at the hunters' camp\030Collect Avanc-meat (total: 8)\030Collect Avanc-skins (total: 10)\030Collect Avanc-tails (total: 12)\tAvanc can be found throughout the Dunbog. Harri has asked you to help him fight the mighty avanc.\n",
[1475]="70030CCF\n1\tFind the pond\tYou find a pond with Orcs and Uruks roaming around, on the move in Fangorn on some errand from Isengard.\n2\tDefeat White Hand Scouts (total: 6)\030Defeat White Hand Uruks (total: 6)\tServants of the White Hand encircle the pond near Oldheart's meadow, polluting the western edge of Fangorn's eaves. You should destroy the hideous servants of the White Hand that harry the forest.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have done well to abate the spread of Saruman's most destructive forces in Fangorn, but the damage cannot be undone. This was an act of revenge, and revenge alone.\n",
[1476]="7001B1F4\n1\tFind Trapjaw\tTrapjaw's lair lies a distance to the north-east of Ivorel's camp in the Scuttledells. Ivorel has tasked you with avenging Hal Tiller by hunting down the deadly black dog, Trapjaw, within the Scuttledells.\n2\tTalk to Ivorel at her camp\tIvorel is at her camp in the Scuttledells, a distance south of Trapjaw's lair. You should speak with Ivorel and tell her that Trapjaw has been slain and that Hal Tiller is alive.\n",
[1477]="7003467C\n1\tFind out what has become of Edsig's Farm\tEdsig's Farm is near Gárferth's Farm, on the road south of Thrymm's Farm. Edsig's Farm was abandoned recently, but most of the Warg-rider attacks seem to have come from that direction.\n2\tDefeat Warg-riders at Edsig's Farm (total: 6)\tWarg-riders are patrolling all over the area near Edsig's Farm. They keep watch on the road, and the surrounding farmlands, so approaching the farm undetected will not be easy.\n3\tCompleted\tThe riders you defeated at Edsig's Farm will go a long way toward avenging those who lost their lives or homes to those Orcs.\n",
[1478]="7003110B\n1\tTell Oldheart what you found\tYou should tell Oldheart of what you found.\n2\tSearch for Léofmar outside of Fangorn\tThe small fishing encampment is on the edge of the Entwash River, where Fangorn meets the Entwash Vale. You should leave Fangorn and make for more inhabited lands, and start by finding your friend Léofmar at the fishing encampment.\n",
[1479]="7005F55A\n1\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost. Determined to both repel the Iron Crown and escort Thrástan to the White Stone Forge, Hermáth Stormhammer has asked you to accompany him and his warriors to Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n2\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Abkân'aban\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn. After defeating Allaban the Collector at Abkân'aban and the revelation of Thrástan's identity, Hermáth Stormhammer wishes to speak with you. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[1480]="7003E457\n1\tWake Treebeard's bog-lurker\030Wake Quickbeam's bog-lurker\030Search for Skinbark's bog-lurker\030Pat Beechbone's bog-lurker to wake it\tBog-lurkers can be found along the Entwash in Fangorn Forest. The Huorn would appreciate your aid in gathering the bog-lurkers that have not gone wild in the absence of the Ents.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have awoken the bog-lurkers and aided Quickbeam's Huorn.\n",
[1481]="70044111\n1\tDouse flaming debris and rescue trapped civilians in Minas Tirith\tA barrage of flaming projectiles loosed by the Enemy's catapults has come crashing down into the First Circle of Minas Tirith, trapping the innocent and setting the city ablaze. You must put out the fires and free the trapped civilians.\n",
[1482]="700442CD\n1\tDouse flaming debris and rescue trapped civilians in Minas Tirith\tA barrage of flaming projectiles loosed by the Enemy's catapults has come crashing down into the First Circle of Minas Tirith, trapping the innocent and setting the city ablaze. You must put out the fires and free the trapped civilians.\n",
[1483]="7005B112\n1\tComplete any 4 of the following quests for the Haban'akkâ of Thráin:\030-'The Great Orc-hunt'\030-'Raid on Rung-shakam'\030-'Blockade on Barazinbar'\030-'Assault on Atrad-zarakh'\030-'The Ufúrzrak Undone'\030-'A Touch of Twistbeard'\030-'Healing the Haban'akkâ'\030-'Warmth Amidst Winter'\030-'Provisions for the Haban'akkâ'\030-'Fuel for the Fires'\030-'Spoils Reclaimed'\030-'Elusive Prey'\tQuests for the Haban'akkâ can be accepted from Thorin or King Thráin at Amdân. Hermáth Stormhammer has suggested that you aid the Haban'akkâ and continue your studies of the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs.\n2\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Amdân. You have continued your studies of the Battle of Azanulbizar. You should return to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[1484]="7002729E\n1\tDefeat Druggavar at the Slade of Shadows (total: 10)\tDruggavar can be found within the Slade of Shadows, south of Andreg's position. Andreg has asked you to defeat the Druggavar summoned by the Old Woman of the Mountain.\n",
[1485]="7003E96D\n1\tSearch for the Ent the Dunlending spoke of outside Isengard\tThe strange tree is rumoured to wander outside the eastern edge of Isengard. The Dunlendings are fleeing in fear from Nan Curunír after being granted freedom by the Ents. They have warned of a tree monster lurking nearby.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam outside Isengard\tQuickbeam can be found to the east of Isengard. The warning of the Dunlendings has turned in your favour, delivering you to an Ent. You should speak with Quickbeam.\n",
[1486]="7003EA66\n1\tSearch for the Ent the Dunlending spoke of outside Isengard\tThe strange tree is rumoured to wander outside the eastern edge of Isengard. The Dunlendings are fleeing in fear from Nan Curunír after being granted freedom by the Ents. They have warned of a tree monster lurking nearby.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam outside Isengard\tQuickbeam can be found to the east of Isengard. The warning of the Dunlendings has turned in your favour, delivering you to an Ent. You should speak with Quickbeam.\n",
[1487]="70045100\n1\tGather lomthond (total: 4)\030Find a walking stick\030Gather lizard-meat (total: 5)\tLomthond can be found near the Falls of Rauros, sticks among the nearby trees, and lizards can be found throughout the Mouths of Entwash. Bring Malhar some lomthond, a walking stick, and some lizard-meat so that he has the strength to make the trek back out of the marshland.\n2\tReturn to Malhar\tReturn to Malhar with the things you gathered, on the hill in the eastern part of Mouths of Entwash.\n",
[1488]="7002C389\n1\tGather reeds from the river's edge (total: 8)\tReeds can be found along the shore of the Great River to the north-east of Brifard's camp. Brifard wants you to gather the reeds that his peasant failed to deliver. He wishes you to return to the wolf-den one last time.\n2\tTalk to Brifard\tBrifard can be found at the camp on the path out of southeastern Thinglad. You should bring the reeds you gathered to Brifard at once.\n",
[1489]="700547A6\n1\tExecute the recipe for guild-pattern leather armour\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Craft guild-pattern leather armour.\n2\tTalk to Hambrennil\030Turn in guild-pattern leather armour (quantity: see journal) to Hambrennil\030Talk to the Tailor's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in guild-pattern leather armour (quantity: see journal) to the Tailor's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[1490]="700547FE\n1\tExecute the recipe for guild-pattern boots\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Forge a pair of guild-pattern boots.\n2\tTalk to Hávar\030Turn in guild-pattern boots (quantity: see journal) to Hávar\030Talk to the Metalsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in guild-pattern boots (quantity: see journal) to the Metalsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[1491]="700547C3\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern chainmail hauberk\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Create a guild-pattern chainmail hauberk.\n2\tTalk to Hávar\030Turn in a guild-pattern chainmail hauberk (quantity: see journal) to Hávar\030Talk to the Metalsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern chainmail hauberk (quantity: see journal) to the Metalsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[1492]="70054800\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern helm\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Forge a guild-pattern helm.\n2\tTalk to Hávar\030Turn in a guild-pattern helm (quantity: see journal) to Hávar\030Talk to the Metalsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern helm (quantity: see journal) to the Metalsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[1493]="700547A8\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern undershirt\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Sew a guild-pattern undershirt.\n2\tTalk to Hambrennil\030Turn in a guild-pattern undershirt (quantity: see journal) to Hambrennil\030Talk to the Tailor's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern undershirt (quantity: see journal) to the Tailor's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[1494]="70054795\n1\tExecute the recipe for guild-pattern leather armour padding\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Craft guild-pattern leather armour padding.\n2\tTalk to Hambrennil\030Turn in guild-pattern leather armour padding (quantity: see journal) to Hambrennil\030Talk to the Tailor's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in guild-pattern leather armour padding (quantity: see journal) to the Tailor's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[1495]="700547FF\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern breastplate\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Forge a guild-pattern breastplate.\n2\tTalk to Hávar\030Turn in a guild-pattern breastplate (quantity: see journal) to Hávar\030Talk to the Metalsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern breastplate (quantity: see journal) to the Metalsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[1496]="700547A7\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern robe\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Sew a guild-pattern robe.\n2\tTalk to Hambrennil\030Turn in a guild-pattern robe (quantity: see journal) to Hambrennil\030Talk to the Tailor's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern robe (quantity: see journal) to the Tailor's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[1497]="70026F07\n1\tTalk to Elder Déin at Lhan Rhos\tLhan Rhos is to the north-west of the hunters' camp. Harri has asked you to return to the village of Lhan Rhos and speak with the Elders there.\n",
[1498]="7003E367\n1\tTalk to Rochwen\tRochwen is encamped near the Last Bridge in the South Trollshaws, far to the south of Thoroniel's camp in the North Trollshaws. Thoroniel bade you carry a report of your campaign against the spiders of the North Trollshaws back to Rochwen.\n",
[1499]="70041D7A\n1\tDefend the pinned citizens\tDefend the citizens from the the Corsair raiders. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[1500]="700428C8\n1\tDefend the pinned citizens\tDefend the citizens from the the Corsair raiders. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[1501]="70032C46\n1\tSearch for Reinn\tReinn tried to get to the Twenty-first Hall from the Great Hall of Durin. You should backtrack from the Twenty-first Hall and search for Reinn, heading south and taking a right along the passage.\n2\tOzût mentioned another Orc involved in Reinn's death. You should search the passages to the Great Hall of Durin for clues to Khîl's whereabouts.\t\n3\tSearch the high platform for a sign of Khîl\tIt is likely that Khîl made his way to the high platform overlooking the centre of the Great Hall of Durin. You should search the high platform for another sign of Khîl.\n4\tSpeak with Mögr nearby, in the Great Hall of Durin\tMögr has followed you to this spot, and stands nearby in silence. You should speak with Mögr.\n",
[1502]="70062DE0\n1\tAlwena's discouraged neighbours could use some encouraging words.\t\n2\tTalk to Alwena outside the Hall of Crafts\tAlwena is outside the Hall of Crafts in Herne.\n3\tTalk to Edhan outside Crossway House\tEdhan is outside the back door of Crossway House.\n4\tTalk to Alwena outside the Hall of Crafts\tAlwena is outside the Hall of Crafts in Herne.\n",
[1503]="70071B35\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai at Onabóha (total: 8)\tYou should defeat Ordâkhai at their encampment at Onabóha to hamper their efforts in the region. Onabóha is located in western An Shêru, just south of Jiret-menêsh.\n2\tCompleted\tYou defeated many Ordâkhai at their encampment at Onabóha, located in western An Shêru, just south of Jiret-menêsh.\n",
[1504]="7003EB9F\n1\tCollect badger-pelts on the High Moor (total: 6)\tBadgers can be found throughout the High Moor, in the Trollshaws. Canaddal has asked you to hunt badgers for their pelts.\n2\tBring the badger-pelts to Canaddal\tCanaddal is posted at the head of the path leading down to the Bruinen Gorges from the High Moor. You should bring the badger-pelts you collected to Canaddal.\n",
